From da2c90d2167d8b2402c007186c6072947d9f6482 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 17:56:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: send the STA_REC before the per-station
 VoW setup

mt7996_mcu_add_sta() issued the VoW DRR control commands for a station
before sending the STA_REC that instantiates it in the firmware. On a
fresh peer entry there is no station context yet, so the firmware
rejects UNI_VOW_DRR_CTRL with 0xC0000001, logging "GetDisablePerStaTx
Failed". That error was returned to the caller, which freed the STA_REC
skb without ever sending it, so bringing up client mode occasionally
failed with "failed to move station to desired state".

Send the STA_REC first and set up the airtime scheduler afterwards.
Airtime fairness is not required for the link to work and the station
record has already been committed at that point, so a failure there no
longer aborts the connection.

Fixes: 910db36ae5b1 ("wifi: mt76: mt7996: HW ATF support")
Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
 mt7996/mcu.c | 15 ++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mt7996/mcu.c b/mt7996/mcu.c
index e6e2bbcd4..176d71e8f 100644
--- a/mt7996/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7996/mcu.c
@@ -3044,14 +3044,15 @@ int mt7996_mcu_add_sta(struct mt7996_dev *dev,
 		}
 	}
 
-	ret = mt7996_mcu_sta_init_vow(dev, &link->mt76, wcid);
-	if (ret) {
-		dev_kfree_skb(skb);
-		return ret;
-	}
 out:
-	return mt76_mcu_skb_send_msg(&dev->mt76, skb,
-				     MCU_WMWA_UNI_CMD(STA_REC_UPDATE), true);
+	ret = mt76_mcu_skb_send_msg(&dev->mt76, skb,
+				    MCU_WMWA_UNI_CMD(STA_REC_UPDATE), true);
+	if (ret || conn_state == CONN_STATE_DISCONNECT)
+		return ret;
+
+	mt7996_mcu_sta_init_vow(dev, &link->mt76, wcid);
+
+	return 0;
 }
 
 int mt7996_mcu_teardown_mld_sta(struct mt7996_dev *dev,
